          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 20:33:51.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrickbot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-10-30 20:33:55.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: shorten replay-single 70c, 70d and 70e",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: shorten replay-single 70c, 70d and 70e\n\nrandom_fail_mdt() slept 120s before each replay barrier, so with\nSLOW=no (180s duration) the tests did one or two MDS failovers\nand took 310-340s, mostly idle time while the load ran.\n\nSleep 30s instead. The load still runs throughout and the tests\nnow do three failovers in about 200s.\n\nMeasured on a rocky9 VM with 2 MDTs, SLOW=no, 2 runs each\n(seconds, before -> after):\n  70c: 310, 239 -> 205, 223\n  70d: 334, 185 -> 192, 189\n  70e: 340, 316 -> 208, 180\nAgainst the roughly 330s CI cost this saves about 120s per run,\nover about 16500 runs per 30 days (70c 6711, 70d and 70e 4900\neach), roughly 550 hours.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=replay-single env=ONLY=\"70c 70d 70e\"\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I8f5df1c8fb504ddc4697244ab7d29d669b9ecd8b\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
